For an Interactive Extension, the Python script connects to a running instance of OpticStudio. Here is the boilerplate using `win32com`:

```python
import win32com.client
import os

class PythonStandaloneApplication(object):
    class LicenseException(Exception):
        pass
    class ConnectionException(Exception):
        pass
    class InitializationException(Exception):
        pass
    class SystemNotPresentException(Exception):
        pass

    def __init__(self):
        self.TheConnection = win32com.client.Dispatch("ZOSAPI.ZOSAPI_Connection")
        self.TheApplication = self.TheConnection.ConnectAsExtension(0)
        if self.TheApplication is None:
            raise PythonStandaloneApplication.ConnectionException("Could not connect to OpticStudio.")
        self.TheSystem = self.TheApplication.PrimarySystem
```
This connects to the first available Interactive Extension (index 0).
